.TH ORO-BACKGROUND-DEFERRED 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:background/deferred \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:background/deferred'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Durable Android reads and registered cleanup/revocation through native executors. Requires `[background] deferred_enabled = true` and native registration from Application.onCreate. Executors resolve references and recheck current server IAM at every attempt. No credentials, request bodies, JS closures or queued arbitrary mutations are accepted. Private origins remain subject to LAN/VPN reachability.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBgetSupport()\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadSupport>\fR
.TP
\fBenqueue(options)\fR
Schedules an authorized native read/reconciliation. Reusing the same task ID with identical options returns its current state, without duplicate delivery. Changing an existing task returns EEXIST. Each attempt has a 60\-second result deadline; a blocked native executor can still occupy the single worker.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (DeferredReadOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadState>\fR
.TP
\fBenqueueMaintenance(options)\fR
Schedules one registered cleanup/revocation task. Registration must explicitly assert retry safety in native code. The executor reauthorizes every attempt and owns idempotency, prerequisites and uncertain\-outcome reconciliation. General mutations, credentials, request bodies and periodic maintenance are rejected. Uses the same journal, five\-attempt budget and cancellation rules.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (DeferredMaintenanceOptions; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadState>\fR
.TP
\fBlist()\fR
Documented function exposed by this module.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadState[]>\fR
.TP
\fBstatus(id)\fR
Reads retained OS scheduling state and the durable last outcome. Interrupted state is explicit and is never silently rescheduled.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIid\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadState>\fR
.TP
\fBresume(id)\fR
Explicitly resumes an interrupted task after app reconciliation. Preserves the five\-attempt budget and replaces its generation, so obsolete callbacks cannot complete the resumed task. The native executor reauthorizes it again.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIid\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadState>\fR
.TP
\fBcancel(id)\fR
Cancels scheduling and signals a running native executor. An already\-running read can finish; its result cannot complete a cancelled or replaced task.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIid\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadState>\fR
.TP
\fBrelease(id)\fR
Cancels and releases a retained task record. Preserve any required application receipt before releasing. A later enqueue of this ID starts a new generation.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIid\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<DeferredReadState>\fR
